  "term": "deep processing",
  "definition": "Deep processing is a thorough, detailed analysis of language input that works toward a full, unambiguous understanding of what a sentence means. In the source, it is contrasted with more superficial “good enough” processing and is described as being used when the task requires that level of analysis.",
